ters retain exact identity while letters lowercase.\",\n+      \"input\": \"A_9-+.:;!?/[]{}'@#=\\u0000\\u001c\\u007fZ\",\n+      \"expected\": [\"a_9-+.:;!?/[]{}'@#=\\u0000\\u001c\\u007fz\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"trailing_escape_after_valid_labels\",\n+      \"intent\": \"A final unpaired escape outside quotes invalidates the whole input even after valid normalized labels.\",\n+      \"input\": \"OK,\\\"GOOD\\\",BAD\\\\\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"trailing_escape_inside_quote\",\n+      \"intent\": \"An unpaired final escape inside quoted mode invalidates the whole input after a valid label.\",\n+      \"input\": \"OK,\\\"BAD\\\\\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"unclosed_quote_after_valid_labels\",\n+      \"intent\": \"An unclosed quote beginning mid-label invalidates the whole input even when earlier labels are valid and commas occur inside the unfinished quote.\",\n+      \"input\": \"OK,GOOD,PRE\\\"BAD,TAIL\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"escaped_final_quote_is_not_closure\",\n+      \"intent\": \"An escaped final quote emits a literal quote and cannot close quoted mode, causing whole-input failure.\",\n+      \"input\": \"OK,\\\"BAD\\\\\\\"\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"escaped_quotes_do_not_open_mode\",\n+      \"intent\": \"Escaped quotes outside quoted mode are literals, leave commas active as separators and do not cause an unclosed-quote error.\",\n+      \"input\": \"\\\\\\\"A,B\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"\",\n+      \"expected\": [\"\\\"a\", \"b\\\"\", \"\\\"\"]\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"properties\": [\"unique_nonempty_labels\", \"ascii_lowercase\"],\n+  \"rationale\": \"These 24 deterministic ASCII cases cover all ten rules and their interactions: separator behavior; quoted/unquoted concatenation; exact one-character escaping of commas, quotes, backslashes, letters and whitespace in both modes; whole-input errors after va